#{[17592186247212 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247212 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111163" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247212 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247212 #edb/ref 1071 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{(1+x+y)^{3}},\\, & 0\\le y\\le x, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X+Y<2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247212 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8656cfbb-6643-57f2-9ab0-17cded63f444" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247212 #edb/ref 1074 "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D={0\\le y\\le x},$ and the event $A={X+Y<2}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](images/f7/f7a0f0fb9d20a4b88d0aa4c395e2adb1d62195601ce756f57a48becc6ab38681.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y<2) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}\\frac{4}{(1+x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}\\frac{4}{(1+x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{2}{(1+x+y)^{2}}]}_{x=y}^{x=2-y}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{2}{(1+2y)^{2}}-\\frac{2}{9})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{1+2y}-\\frac{2y}{9}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{9}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247213 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186246986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247213 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111167" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247213 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247213 #edb/ref 1071 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X+Y>1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247213 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5199c42f-aff1-55e5-b62b-a83ffcaa9370" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247213 #edb/ref 1074 "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,1]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A={X+Y>1}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](images/58/58c1beb1b13680e330260d93fdf8e60460e2bfeae4c1cbbc2fce8b261afe7ea1.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y>1) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{A}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371569 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371569 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111251" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371569 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371569 #edb/ref 1071 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(Y<X<Y+2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371569 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "821858ee-46eb-57a4-9f6b-cec1ae6e7ca5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371569 #edb/ref 1074 "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,3]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A={Y<X<Y+2}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](images/f4/f4a0cc357eee835c84ef08524d27e3c30b98d58e1b6b5083b7df6a66ce987b6b.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<X<Y+2) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{A}\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371570 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371570 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371570 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186371571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371570 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "63d8ef8e-e282-5085-bd0c-37645c87d08b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371571 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371571 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371571 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "58338181-f5f2-53c4-ba2c-1eea5f78b0ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371572 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371572 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371572 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "51c241d2-b827-5429-8bbc-12cb2e50febb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371573 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371573 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371573 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08d78c40-67ca-5552-bfbc-85ea24759319" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371574 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371574 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371574 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6cfd8f25-4f0e-55fd-8077-79f56797ab4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371575 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 1759218604541